  "articleBody": "It's easy to make a few common blunders when maintaining a rental property that can end up costing you big bucks down the line. One frequent mistake is delaying small leaks. That tiny drip might seem harmless, but it can lead to massive water damage and mold issues if ignored. Another big one is skipping HVAC servicing. Regular checks keep your systems running efficiently and prevent breakdowns when you least expect them, saving you from expensive emergency repairs. Not keeping good records is another trap. Documentation of repairs, inspections, and communication with tenants is super important, especially if disputes come up. Also, failing to clarify who's responsible for routine upkeep, like clearing drains or reporting pests, can cause headaches. You don't want tenants ignoring problems because they're unsure if it's their job to report it. HH Remodeling LLC understands these challenges and can help address many of these common maintenance items before they turn into bigger, more expensive issues. Get ahead of these problems; it'll save you stress and money!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
